# Generated projection output. Ignored, with two exceptions: the dbt package and the
# architecture diagrams.
#
# `ontology-hub-publish/medallion/dbt` must stay tracked because a dataplatform
# consumes it as a dbt package pinned by `git` + `revision` + `subdirectory`, which
# `dbt deps` resolves out of the *committed* tree at that tag. Untracked, the path
# does not exist at the revision and `dbt deps` fails outright -- and DD-206 §4 wants
# a release to publish exactly the bytes reviewed and merged at the tagged commit,
# which pr-validate.yml enforces by regenerating and diffing it before merge.
#
# `ontology-hub-publish/architecture` is tracked for a different reason: the canonical
# class diagrams and DDD maps are how the model gets reviewed and explained, so a
# reviewer should see them change in a pull request rather than regenerate locally to
# find out. Left untracked they rot invisibly -- one hub's had drifted into mixed
# vintages, some domains regenerated weeks apart, and nothing surfaced it because
# nothing was watching. pr-validate.yml regenerates and diffs this path, so tracking it
# is load-bearing rather than decorative (#774).
#
# Everything else is ignored, the Power BI PBIP output included: it used to be
# allowlisted for the release lane, but `package-powerbi-release` renders and zips it
# in CI from the compile plan, so nothing needs it committed. Every other target
# (neo4j, azure-search, a2ui, prompt, mdm, reports/details) is an
# alternate export, and reports/details can carry PII-adjacent validation detail.
#
# The Silver and declared-contract ERDs are not here. They are written into the
# *authored* tree, at `ontology-hub/model/contracts/diagrams/`, beside the contracts
# they are drawn from. Same reasoning as the architecture diagrams above -- a diagram
# is the one generated artifact a human actually reviews, so it has to be visible in
# the pull request -- only the destination differs.
#
# Track anything more only after a deliberate, per-hub review (see CICD.md), never by
# widening this default silently.
ontology-hub-publish/**
!ontology-hub-publish/**/
!ontology-hub-publish/**/.gitkeep
!ontology-hub-publish/medallion/dbt/**
!ontology-hub-publish/architecture/**

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Raw client evidence (toolkit-created convention). Matched as `**/.import/*` rather
# than `.import/` so the negation below can apply -- git never descends into a
# directory matched by a bare `dir/` pattern, so `.import/modeling/` could not
# otherwise be un-ignored (#591).
**/.import/*
# ...except toolkit-managed, structured records under .import/modeling/ (#591) --
# these are OKF-style records with their own provenance, not disposable exports.
!**/.import/modeling/

# Toolkit performance caches (analyse-sources/propose-alignment, ontology-closure parse
# cache) -- content-hash keyed, safe to delete anytime, never affects compiled output
.cache/

# Toolkit run logs and local state (per-run JSON-lines diagnostics, #1011)
.kairos/

